# AxizPOS dates

All date inputs and date displays use `DD-MM-YYYY`. A page must not introduce another numeric date format.

Use `AxizDatePicker` from `@ai-pos/ui` for every date field. `DateInput` and `TextField type="date"` are the same picker. Use `AxizDateRange` for a From/To pair. Use `withTime` or `variant="datetime"` when the value includes a time, and show that as `DD-MM-YYYY HH:mm`.

Do not use `<input type="date">` or `<input type="datetime-local">`. The browser's own date control changes its visible format with the operating system.

Store date-only values as `YYYY-MM-DD`. Do not parse them with `new Date("YYYY-MM-DD")` and do not format them with `toLocaleDateString`. Use `formatDate`, `parseDate`, and `formatDateTime` from `@ai-pos/ui`.

`formatDate` prints the calendar date written in the string. `formatDateTime` prints an instant in a timezone. A time-only control may stay `<input type="time">`.

Month names in a calendar, and a month-year period heading, may stay localized. The number in the field stays `DD-MM-YYYY` in English and Arabic.

```tsx
<AxizDatePicker
  aria-label="Date"
  value={spentOn}
  onChange={(event) => setSpentOn(event.target.value)}
/>
```
